WEBVTT

00:03.920 --> 00:06.680
Okay, so now what is exactly a left anti-join.

00:06.720 --> 00:12.600
Now, in this mechanism, we want to return rows from the left side, the left table that has no match

00:12.640 --> 00:13.720
in the right table.

00:13.720 --> 00:19.520
So now by looking to our two circles from the left table, we want to see only the unmatching rows.

00:19.520 --> 00:25.920
So only rows that exist in table A, but it don't exist in the table B so if there is like matching

00:25.920 --> 00:27.480
data we don't want to see it.

00:27.480 --> 00:29.920
And now from the right table we don't want anything.

00:29.920 --> 00:31.360
We don't want any data.

00:31.360 --> 00:34.720
So that means the only source of your data is going to be the left table.

00:34.720 --> 00:35.760
And from the right table.

00:35.760 --> 00:37.040
We don't need any data.

00:37.040 --> 00:40.520
We are just joining the tables to do a check to filter the data.

00:40.560 --> 00:41.680
So now for the syntax.

00:41.680 --> 00:42.800
This is going to be interesting.

00:42.800 --> 00:45.680
We don't have a special type called left anti-join.

00:45.720 --> 00:48.840
At least in the SQL server we still can create this effect.

00:48.880 --> 00:54.320
Since we are saying left we can use the type left join and then as usual the join condition with the

00:54.360 --> 00:54.720
keys.

00:54.720 --> 00:58.400
But now if you leave it like this, you will get the effect of the left join.

00:58.400 --> 01:03.040
And we don't want that because with the left join you will get the complete circle from the left table.

01:03.080 --> 01:07.880
But now in order to remove the matching data, this overlapping in the middle, what we can do.

01:07.880 --> 01:12.080
We can use a filter and in order to filter the data we use the Where clause.

01:12.080 --> 01:17.640
So now in order to get rid of the matching data, we can take the key from the right table.

01:17.640 --> 01:20.200
And we say the key must be null.

01:20.200 --> 01:21.600
So if the key is null.

01:21.600 --> 01:24.760
So that means there is no match on the right side.

01:24.760 --> 01:30.360
And if you do it like this, you will get the effect of the left anti-join only the data in the left

01:30.360 --> 01:32.360
that has no match on the right.

01:32.360 --> 01:35.000
So now let's go and scale and create this effect.

01:35.040 --> 01:36.480
Okay, so now we have the following task.

01:36.520 --> 01:40.040
And it says get all customers who haven't placed any order.

01:40.080 --> 01:44.120
So now by looking to this query clearly we are focusing on the table customers.

01:44.120 --> 01:47.320
But we want to see the customers that didn't order anything.

01:47.320 --> 01:51.000
So they are in our database but the customers are inactive now.

01:51.000 --> 01:55.560
There are like different ways on how to solve this task, but we're going to solve it using the joins.

01:55.600 --> 02:01.520
Now let's go and start by just writing a very simple query where we are selecting everything from the

02:01.520 --> 02:02.590
table customers.

02:02.630 --> 02:04.950
Now you can see this is our five customers.

02:04.990 --> 02:08.630
And now I want to check which of those customers didn't order anything yet.

02:08.670 --> 02:12.790
Now since we are talking about the orders, we can go and join it with the table orders.

02:12.790 --> 02:17.550
So we're going to say left join the table orders as oh, and then we're going to go and connect the

02:17.550 --> 02:21.430
tables using the IDs with the customer ID.

02:21.430 --> 02:26.350
So now if we go and execute it now we are still seeing all the customers because we are using the left

02:26.350 --> 02:26.750
join.

02:26.750 --> 02:30.390
And now we can see the orders informations of each customer.

02:30.390 --> 02:36.270
And you can see immediately those two customers didn't order anything because we are seeing here nulls.

02:36.270 --> 02:36.750
Right.

02:36.750 --> 02:37.750
So they are empty.

02:37.790 --> 02:38.910
There is no orders.

02:38.950 --> 02:42.590
Now we can use this information in order to filter the data.

02:42.590 --> 02:44.870
I just want to see Martin and Peter.

02:44.870 --> 02:47.830
So what we can do, we can go and say where and all.

02:47.830 --> 02:51.950
What you have to do is to take the key that we are using in order to join the tables.

02:51.950 --> 02:55.710
This is this one over here and say this must be null.

02:55.710 --> 02:57.430
So is null.

02:57.430 --> 03:00.270
So if you see it like this, that means you want to see the data.

03:00.270 --> 03:01.870
If the customer ID is null.

03:01.870 --> 03:04.070
So let's go and execute it.

03:04.110 --> 03:04.790
Perfect.

03:04.830 --> 03:08.190
Now you are getting the customers who haven't ordered anything.

03:08.190 --> 03:10.630
And this is exactly the effect that we wanted.

03:10.630 --> 03:11.830
The lift antijoin.

03:11.870 --> 03:17.030
We are getting the data from the left side where there are no match on the right side.

03:17.030 --> 03:18.910
So you have always to do it in two steps.

03:18.950 --> 03:24.790
First, join the data as you normally do using the classical joins the left join and then the second

03:24.790 --> 03:27.990
step you go and use a filter using the Where clause.

03:27.990 --> 03:31.030
If you do it like this, you can check for not existence.

03:31.030 --> 03:34.150
And with that we are getting the effect of the lift antijoin.

03:34.190 --> 03:35.070
So that's it.

03:35.110 --> 03:39.910
Okay, so now if you are looking to this picture, I think you already know where we use the lift Antijoin

03:39.910 --> 03:43.830
we can use it only on the last use case where we are checking the existence.

03:43.830 --> 03:49.070
So if we use the lift join together with the where you can check for the not existence of your data

03:49.070 --> 03:50.030
in another table.

03:50.070 --> 03:52.150
So this is exactly for this scenario.

03:52.190 --> 03:52.590
All right.

03:52.590 --> 03:54.670
So that's all about the lift Antijoin.

03:54.710 --> 03:57.550
Now we're going to speak about the exact opposite of that.

03:57.590 --> 03:59.950
We will cover the right antijoin.

03:59.950 --> 04:03.030
So it can be very similar but we are just switching sides.

04:03.030 --> 04:03.830
So let's go.
